<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramanatha (Hoysala)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1263–1295</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramanatha was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysala</a> king who ruled the Tamil territories of the kingdom from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannanur-kuppam">Kannanur Kuppam</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srirangam">Srirangam</a>, after his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vira-someshwara">Vira Someshvara</a> divided his lands. His rivalry with his half-brother Narasimha III in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a> led to war between them. Pandyan advances drove him from the Tamil country, and he ended his reign in southern Karnataka.</p></div>
